.TH DCC-CPU-DAEMON 8 2026-11-22 "Dudes Control Center @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.nh
.SH NAME
dcc-cpu-daemon, dcc-hard-limit-enforce \- CPU frequency daemon of Dudes Control Center
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcc-cpu-daemon
.RB [ \-\-foreground | \-f ]
.br
.B dcc-hard-limit-enforce
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dcc-cpu-daemon
runs as root from
.BR dcc-cpu-daemon.service .
It sets the CPU governor and the minimum and maximum frequency of each core
through
.IR /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq ,
applies CPU profiles and keeps every core at or below the hard frequency
limit.
Profiles and the hard limit come from the desktop user's
.I profiles.json
(see
.BR dudes-control-center (7));
on start the daemon applies the hard limit to all cores.
.PP
Clients connect to
.IR /run/dcc-cpu.sock ;
only root and members of the group
.B dudes-control-center
are accepted.
.PP
.B dcc-hard-limit-enforce
is a fail-safe that works without the daemon:
.B dcc-hard-limit-enforcer.timer
runs it every 10 seconds (first 10 seconds after boot).
It reads the hard limit from
.I profiles.json
with the rights of that file's owner and lowers every core whose maximum
frequency is above it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-foreground ", " \-f
Stay in the foreground (the service uses this).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dcc-cpu.sock
Command socket.
.TP
.I /var/log/dudes-control-center/CPU_DAEMON.log
Daemon log (rotated at 1 MB, 5 old files kept).
.TP
.I /var/log/dudes-control-center/HARD_LIMIT_ENFORCER.log
Log of the fail-safe (capped at 1 MB).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/dcc-cpu-daemon.service
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/dcc-hard-limit-enforcer.service
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/dcc-hard-limit-enforcer.timer
Units; none of them starts while
.I /etc/dudes-control-center/disabled-cpu
exists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DCC_PROFILES_PATH
Absolute path of the
.I profiles.json
to use, for example set in a systemd drop-in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dudes-control-center (7),
.BR dcc-cpu-cli (1),
.BR dcc-gui (1),
.BR dcc-component (8),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
